course: dictionary
lesson: 1758
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing. Clean is one of them. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants. «The bird bathed to keep its feathers clean.» Here clean means not dirty.
explain: Look at «The satanic leaf-tailed gecko licks its eyes clean.» Licking takes the dirt away, so here clean is a job: to clean means to take the dirt away. Ask yourself what action the sentence describes, and that helps you find the meaning.
explain: Clean can also mean completely, as in «I clean forgot». The word forgot tells you what kind of clean this is. Try the meaning in the sentence. Does «I completely forgot» make sense? Then you have found it.
fact: Clean has more than one meaning, so check the sentence around it.
fact: «Clean» can mean not dirty, or it can mean to take the dirt away.
fact: «Clean» can mean fresh and unused, as in a clean sheet of paper.
fact: «Clean» can mean fair and following the rules, as in a clean game.
fact: Phrases with clean include clean up, clean water and come clean, which means to tell the truth.
exercise: Mila wants to start her story on a clean sheet of paper. What does clean mean here? | Taking the dirt away | Not dirty with mud | *Fresh and unused | Completely
exercise: «Birds bathe to keep their feathers clean and working well.» What does clean mean in this sentence? | Completely | Fresh and unused, like a new book | *Not dirty | Fair and following the rules
exercise: Ben says, «I clean forgot my bag!» What does clean mean in his sentence? | *Completely | Not dirty | Fair and following the rules | To take the dirt away
test: «The gecko licks its eyes clean.» What does clean mean in this sentence? | Completely | *To take the dirt away | Fresh and unused | Fair and following the rules
test: Which phrase means to tell the truth? | Clean energy | *Come clean | Clean up | Clean water
exam: Which meaning of clean fits best in «The referee said it was a clean game»? | To take the dirt away | Not dirty | *Fair and following the rules | Completely
